  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'when you finally headshot 150 black people' because the phrase 'you' directly addresses the viewer, creating an implicit 'you' as the subject performing the violent action. This deictic pronoun 'you' anchors the user's identity as the perpetrator in the meme's hateful narrative, projecting the user onto the text as the agent of the described violence.",
